// Nomu standard library — core (task 174).
//
// The native boundary + non-user-facing GC substrate: the types the compiler/runtime name but user programs
// do not. The user-facing surface (`Option`, `Result`, `String`, `concat`, the numeric helpers, `Time`,
// `SimpleRNG`, and future collections / IO) lives in the `std` package (moved there by the 174.3 content
// split). `core` is importable only from `std` (modules.md §Imports): user code reaches it through `std`.

// A managed, relocatable single-object buffer: a fixed `Header` plus a variable-length tail of `Element`,
// in one allocation (`{ type-id, cap, Header, Element[cap] }`). The shared storage primitive under `Array`,
// heap `String`, and a future `Dictionary` (task 180, design/plans/tasks/180-managed-buffer.md). An ordinary
// generic reference type for the type system; its four operations (`create`, `capacity`, `headerPtr`,
// `elementPtr`) are compiler intrinsics — the magic is the tail-allocation + the GC descriptor, confined
// there. Header and element access is raw (`RawPtr`); consumers build typed, bounds-checked APIs on top.
public class ManagedBuffer<Header, Element> {
}

// `EmptyHeader` (the zero-field `ManagedBuffer` header for a buffer needing no per-buffer metadata beyond
// `cap` — heap `String` storage is a `ManagedBuffer<EmptyHeader, UInt8>`) is a compiler builtin (task
// 174.5.1): codegen names it, it carries no symbols, and it is never written in source, so the egress seeds
// its zero-field layout directly rather than a prepended decl.
